Z||000003||fierojp||11-10-2001||02:05 PM||||I had an MSD 6A on my Formula.  It cost 129 plus like 10 bucks for a wiring harness.  Easy install and the car seemed to run smoother.  It's hard to say if there was a performance increase, but I would guess there was a slight benefit.  With this system, you can also slightly enlarge your spark plug gaps, which will also help performance.<P>JP||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-10-2001||07:03 PM||||If you are just doing the module get a GM one.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-10-2001||07:20 PM||||Count me in as one of the faithfuls for GM.  Need a single replacement part - get GM Delco!  <P>I have 123K on an original - no unscheduled maintenance (yeah, the usual oil/filter, tires, battery, alternator, timing chain, sensors, etc) engine/transmission/electrical - all original GM and still running like new.<P>Going to install a whole new system - do your research and install what you want/need.||||reg||10
